    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/owner/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 A small helper `TelephoneDisplay.of(String e164)` that splits off the country code (1 digit for `+1`, 2 digits otherwise, mirroring how `OwnerTelephone` treats country codes) then groups the national digits in threes: `\"+61412345678\"` \u2192 `\"+61 412 345 678\"`. It returns the input unchanged for null/non-E.164 values.\n\n3. **`.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` computed from `owner.getTelephone()`, alongside the existing derived fields.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (asserting `telephone` = `+61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`) passes, and the full test suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
